
 *
 * Commodore compatible Matrix Printer Emulator.
 *
 * Restricted Epson compatible Serial printer emulator.
 * Only text mode is supported.
 *
 * Written by
 *   Jarkko Sonninen  (sonninen@lut.fi)
 *   Jouko Valta     (jopi@stekt.oulu.fi)
 *   Hannu Helminen  (dm@stekt.oulu.fi)

This is a small program to convert CBM printer output to 
a postscript file that, when fed to a postscript printer, 
produces a nice image of a matrix printer - a Matrix printer
emulation.

It used to be part of the X64/VICE emulator project, however
the copyright of petlp.c forbid using it when we cleaned up the VICE code:

[...section removed...]

It can now compiled separately from the VICE emulator
(in fact it's just a shameless rip from VICE 0.11.0).
It is only tested on Unix (anyone care for DOS/Win)?

In the newer VICE versions you can (under Unix) even use it
by using "|petlp -F PS|lpr" as the printer output file - which 
automatically pipes the output through "petlp" and then to the
(default) printer via "lpr".

Andre Fachat
a.fachat@physik.tu-chemnitz.de


--------------------------------------------------

   ./petlp V1.00 -- Commodore Matrix Printer Emulator.

Usage: ./petlp  [-c | -nc] [-latin | -graph ] [-lang langname ]
        [-upper | -lower | -business ]
        [-left n ] [-right n ] [-top n ] [-bot n ]
        [-o outfile ] [-F format ] [-P printer ] [--] [file list]


   -c           controls (interpret also control codes)
   -nc          no controls (suppress control codes in printout)
   -upper       select graphics character set
   -lower       select business character set
   -business    select business character set
   -lang        specify International character set
   -ascii       select ASCII input (resets -lang to US-ASCII)
   -latin       same as -ascii
   -F output-format

Available output formats are:
binary log petcii ascii Latin/1 PS 

